cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "juliaTDGL: three-dimensional multiband time-dependent Ginzburg-Landau solvers"
message: >
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Robles Calderón
    given-names: Jorge Alfredo
    alias: georgeotjg
    affiliation: Universidad Nacional de Colombia
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-0557-0263"
abstract: >
  Three-dimensional time-dependent Ginzburg-Landau solvers in Julia for the geometric
  superconducting diode effect in two-gap superconductors (MgB2 as target). Release 2.0:
  N bands with Kramer-Watts-Tobin relaxation per band (the charge imbalance at the contacts),
  normal fluids per band, thermal noise, regions of different materials, sculpted samples,
  stabilised Runge-Kutta-Chebyshev stages and a rotating frame for the stiff bands, open and bar
  boundaries for the self-field, an insulating buffer, and the onset by the delay of the first phase slip;
  with the new terms off it reproduces release 1.2. Release 1.2, the two-band solver:
  link variables, self-consistent vector potential, optional scalar potential by Coulomb
  projection, Josephson voltmeter with a crossing-count verdict rule, and a production scheme
  with the curl-curl term implicit and the light band in substeps. Optional terms, all off
  by default, add interband drag, a temperature field with Joule heating, a diffused gauge
  residual and a bath temperature.
keywords:
  - time-dependent Ginzburg-Landau
  - superconducting diode effect
  - two-band superconductivity
  - multiband superconductivity
  - Kramer-Watts-Tobin
  - MgB2
  - vortex dynamics
  - Julia
